%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Notification helper uses its actual client. Do not infer distributed or outbox atomicity from the enclosing transaction.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Receptionist
    participant UI as API client
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as attendance.controller.ts
    participant S as receptionAttendanceService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Send warning for selected member and class
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/attendance/warnings/send
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorizeExact(RECEPTIONIST, MANAGER)
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: sendReceptionWarning(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: sendReceptionAttendanceWarning(user, input)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Begin transaction, read current member / class attendance detail under relevant lock
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Require absence rate at least 20 percent
        S->>S: If an earlier warning for this class exists, return alreadySent without another notification
        alt pair inaccessible or below warning threshold
            S->>DB: Roll back transaction
            S-->>C: 400 / 403 / 404
        else business conditions satisfied
            alt previous warning exists
                S-->>C: alreadySent true with original sentAt
            else first valid request
                S->>DB: Create ATTENDANCE_WARNING only if not previously sent
                activate DB
                DB-->>S: Saved result
                deactivate DB
                S->>DB: Commit transaction
                S-->>C: alreadySent indicator and original or new sentAt
            end
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error
